      "content": "<|channel>thought\n<channel|>those are good starting points. but i feel like they're a bit focused on how we treat other people. what about personal qualities that focus more on the individual's relationship to the state or their own duties? like, i've seen some people arguing that things like personal responsibility or respecting tradition are just as important for a stable society. do those still count as virtues in a modern democracy, or are they outdated?",
